(collections-c, batch C (night) - docs/ledger/collections-a.md rows
 LST-04, LST-43, LST-45, LST-46, LST-47 and collections-b.md rows
 LST2-30, LST2-41, LST2-46, LST2-53, LST2-94.

 Each leaf is called directly off a pinned rng seed and its emitted
 source printed in full, the same convention tests/390_gen_collections_b.vox
 uses. Each leaf is also emitted nested at least once, since 'gen join
 lines' renders a nested body (comma-joined) differently from a
 top-level one (period-joined) and that difference is exactly what a
 leaf's own gate has to prove survives rendering, not just "the idea"
 of the leaf (PROCEDURE.md 6a).

 The naming allocator for most of these leaves is 'gen buffer
 name'/'gen buffer reference'/'gen buffer property'/'gen buffer
 companion' from gen_buffers.vox - reused rather than re-spent, per
 tonight's brief. 'gen leaf map missing key typed default' is the one
 exception: it reuses 'gen fresh noun'/'gen written name'/'gen
 possessive name' instead, the same idiom 'gen leaf absent key' (VAL-27)
 already uses for this exact shape - a map, a missing key, an `On
 error` witness - because a possessive built off an already-quoted
 buffer-companion name would double its own closing quote.)

Print "--- LST-43, LST-45: insert and replace, same map ---".
'rng seed' of 1.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf map insert and replace' of "" and false.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- the same leaf, nested ---".
'rng seed' of 1.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf map insert and replace' of "  " and true.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- LST-46: length and empty, an empty map and a populated one ---".
'rng seed' of 1.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf map length and empty' of "" and false.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- the same leaf, nested ---".
'rng seed' of 1.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf map length and empty' of "  " and true.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- LST-04: an empty list, length 0 and empty true before any append ---".
'rng seed' of 1.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf list empty state' of "" and false.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- the same leaf, nested ---".
'rng seed' of 1.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf list empty state' of "  " and true.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- LST-47: keys/values order and freshness, a two-key map ---".
'rng seed' of 1.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf map keys values fresh' of "" and false.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- the same leaf, a three-key map ---".
'rng seed' of 7.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf map keys values fresh' of "" and false.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- the same leaf, nested ---".
'rng seed' of 1.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf map keys values fresh' of "  " and true.
Print 'gen text'.

